{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/121968-combat-with-ghosts","id":121968,"title":"Combat with Ghosts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-29T14:00:38-07:00","id":121968,"title":"Combat with Ghosts","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> Geist seems like the unloved child of the nWOD line and the other weekend I took the time to try to read it carefully and get an idea of how it works. It seems that they deal with ghosts the same way that Werewolves deal with unruly spirits. I did have some questions on how conflict can occur. Here were some musings...<br /> <br /> 1/ Can you ever hit a ghost that is either manifest or unmanifested? If it is unmanifested I guess it is invisible and in the land of the dead. Does being Manifested mean that it appears and you can hit it or does only a blessed weapon work? Some Stigmata powers seem to affect Unmanifested ghosts, does that mean that they are the only ones that affect manifested ghosts or can other powers like claws affect a ghost that has appeared?<br /> <br /> 2/ In the scenario &quot;through the ebon gate&quot; there is a fight scene where a bunch of Sin Eaters are attacked by a group of ghosts. It mentions that the anchors are near. Does that suggest that the fight involves sin eaters looking for anchors to destroy while ghosts are throwing things at them? Can a sin eater go toe to toe with a ghost and engage in hand to hand combat? I know that there is a power of sin eaters where they can shift into twilight to fight ghosts with their bare hands, is that what sin eaters can do to engage ghosts on their own turf?<br /> <br /> 3/ Ghostly powers to affect the living seem really lame. Telekinesis suggests that a ghost rolls his dice pool and the successes will be his strength to make physical attacks. That means a dice pool of 7 results in a strength of 2 or 3. I guess that is the same strength as a normal human...<br /> <br /> 4/ Which sin eater powers actually affect ghosts? Does it need to be a stigmata manifestation or will any powers act like blessed weapons? If a sin eater with a primeval manifestation grows claws can he hit a manifested ghost? Alternatively, can he grow the claws and then move to twilight to attack the ghost more effectively?<br /> <br /> 5/ In the Underworld, are all ghosts solid so they are treated like normal people?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T16:55:00-07:00","id":122088,"title":"","content":"Are you using GMC rules?<br /> <br /> 5. They're treated as solid in the Underworld, yep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T09:53:51-07:00","id":122422,"title":"","content":"The rules I've always understood them and used them for Geist go like this:<br /> <br /> 1 &amp; 4) A ghost which is manifested may both interact with solid objects and be interacted with. Purely mortal characters may have more trouble (requiring a blessed weapon), but Sin-Eaters (by virtue of being part ghost-ish) are able to interact with Manifested ghosts as though they were solid; all of their powers affect them normally at this point.<br /> When a ghost has not manifested, it is in a state called 'Twilight' - invisible, intangible, but hanging out in this world. Sin-Eaters can always see and talk to ghosts, even if they're in Twilight, but touching them becomes tricky. The Stigmata Shroud is the best way to do this, by a mile. However, all Sin-Eaters can spend 1 Plasm to do a &quot;reverse possession&quot; of their geist, allowing them to physically interact with Twilight beings: no weapons or items work, except for their keystone, but they can use any 'natural weapons' - including claws, or possibly items they've inserted with Industrial Caul. They can even grapple a ghosts possessing someone and yank them out (always loved that bit). Their body is still physical though (they're kind of in both worlds at once), so any bystanders at risk, especially because they can't see the physical too well while doing this.<br /> <br /> If you are using <b>GMC</b> era rules, then ghosts all have a Rank and a Bane (also a ban), and Sin-Eaters have an honorary rank (although they haven't said how this is calculated yet; your storyteller would need to decide on that). A ghost's Bane is <i>always </i>tangible to them: while in Twilight, touching their Bane (which is a physical object) deals 1 Lethal per round or attack damage if its used that way; when they're manifested, the Bane deals Aggravated (which also depletes Essence equal to the damage) [see page 221 of GMC for the rules and examples; also 218 for the Rank chart]. The really neat part is that if a Sin-Eater's honorary rank is two higher than a ghost's, their natural weapons count as the ghost's Bane. So, if a character has the honorary ghost rank of 3, any rank 1 ghosts she finds (the majority in the material world) can be attacked in Twilight, and with grievous damage if they manifest to fight back.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes; that scene does imply that seeking out the anchors will be one effective way to resolve the fight. If the anchors are found, they can either be destroyed, banishing the ghosts to the Underworld (or at least to a different anchor), or used to threaten the specters and possibly negotiate with. That being said, the Sin-Eaters can probably go toe-to-toe with them anyway. Which gets into point number...<br /> <br /> 3) Ghost powers do seem fairly weak, as does their attribute spread. You can always buff them, make them higher rank, or give access to new Numina (maybe the Sin-Eaters own powers, maybe spirit stuff, or whatever neat thing you come up with). As it stands, though, Sin-Eaters can stomp over most of the ghosts they meet on a regular basis; they are very powerful, especially compared to your average ghost. They're more supposed to help ghosts finish their business rather than fight them, though. The antagonists which actually threaten Sin-Eaters are ghosts from the Underworld (they start getting real powerful at mid rank 3) and unfettered geists.<br /> <br /> 5) Yes; everything in the Underworld is treated as solid, as it does not have a state of Twilight (most Other Worlds are like this).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 04-30-2014, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T18:27:59-07:00","id":185915,"title":"","content":"The rules for how geists can affect ghosts are still a bit confusing I get reverse possession, a sin eater can go into twilight to attack a ghost in twilight with his bare hands or any improvised weapons he finds How about a ghost that manifested? Do the fists of a sin eater count as blessed weapons? How about a mundane sword he is carrying? Would that affect a ghost? Or.. Are sin eaters just like other mortals and need to rely on wits like mortals, or use their powers to affect ghosts? I am just curious because I cannot see how a sin eater can harm a manifested ghost, unless the GMC rules say that mundane weapons can affect ghosts now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T19:38:35-07:00","id":185948,"title":"","content":"Ok... I think I get it, a ghost who has manifested is still in a twilight state but the ghost can interact with the mortal world in a better way. Reverse possession is the most common way for Sin eaters to fight ghosts in a physical manner. Using an ak47 is not allowed, but growing claws by using a primeval manifestation is fair game. Mementos are used as weapons. In the physical realm, taking out an anchor can take out the ghost itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T12:26:15-07:00","id":186449,"title":"","content":"What happens if a ghost dies? If a solid ghost in the underworld is hit by a truck, what's the result?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T12:37:14-07:00","id":186452,"title":"","content":"If 'killed' in the underworld, they appear as though a corpse for about 24 hours until they would normally gain Essence from being Down Below; at that point, they heal one health box, and go about their lives. If they run out of Essence while having health left, they turn into an intangible state (as if in Twilight) - still visible, but unable to physically interact with anything until they gain a point back. As usual, only depleting health and essence both will destroy them permanently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}